The internal representation can change from `double` to `BigDecimal`, from one field to a transaction ledger — **no caller changes**.

```java
// Trying to model AmphibiousVehicle via inheritance
class Vehicle { ... }
class Car   extends Vehicle { ... }  // IS-A Vehicle ✓
class Boat  extends Vehicle { ... }  // IS-A Vehicle ✓

// AmphibiousVehicle IS-A Car AND IS-A Boat?
// Java = single inheritance only — you must pick one.
class AmphibiousVehicle extends Car { ... }  // ✗ not a Boat
class AmphibiousVehicle extends Boat { ... } // ✗ not a Car
// No correct answer exists. The hierarchy collapses.
```

```java
class AmphibiousVehicle {
    private CarDrive  carDrive  = new CarDrive();   // HAS-A
    private BoatDrive boatDrive = new BoatDrive();  // HAS-A

    public void drive() { carDrive.drive(); }  // delegate
    public void sail()  { boatDrive.sail(); }  // delegate
}
// Swap CarDrive → ElectricCarDrive: zero impact on boatDrive.
// No inheritance needed. No hierarchy to collapse.
```

When the IS-A test fails, reach for composition (HAS-A). Inherit behavior only when the relationship is genuinely permanent.

